{
  "name": "PetNord — Aito Predictive E-commerce Tour",
  "description": "A guided, runnable tour of the queries behind the PetNord demo: picked-for-you ranking with $why, smart search, cross-sell, churn, product filling, offers, win-back and review triage. Every query is run against the demo data before it is published.",
  "sections": [
    {
      "title": "Start here",
      "widgets": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "title": "What this workbook is",
          "size": "full",
          "config": {
            "content": "# PetNord — Aito Predictive E-commerce Tour\n\nPetNord is a fictional pet-supplies retailer. This workbook walks through the Aito queries behind its demo app (ecommerce.aito.ai); every query is **runnable**: hit *Run*, then edit the query and run again.\n\nThe data is synthetic and relational: `customers` → `contexts` (one per visit) → `impressions` (what was shown, and whether it was bought), `orders`, `products` → `product_states` (a product's price, offer and rating in one month), `reviews`, `winback_campaigns`, `customer_months`. Links such as `context.customer.pets` or `product_state.discount_band` follow those relations inside a query.\n\nTwo habits worth copying: ask for `$p` (a calibrated probability) and for `$why` (what each part of the context contributed to it)."
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "metrics",
          "title": "Instance activity",
          "size": "full",
          "config": {
            "displayFields": [
              "status",
              "lastRequest",
              "requests5min",
              "requests1hr",
              "memory",
              "disk"
            ],
            "refreshIntervalSeconds": 30
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "1 · Explore the data",
      "widgets": [
        {
          "type": "query",
          "title": "Browse the product catalog",
          "size": "full",
          "config": {
            "query": {
              "from": "products",
              "limit": 10
            },
            "endpoint": "query",
            "displayMode": "playground",
            "outputFormat": "table",
            "runPolicy": "onLoad"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "query",
          "title": "Customers in one region",
          "size": "full",
          "config": {
            "query": {
              "from": "customers",
              "where": {
                "region": "helsinki"
              },
              "limit": 10
            },
            "endpoint": "query",
            "displayMode": "playground",
            "outputFormat": "table",
            "runPolicy": "manual"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "query",
          "title": "Average order value across all orders",
          "size": "full",
          "config": {
            "query": {
              "from": "orders",
              "aggregate": [
                "total_eur.$mean",
                "total_eur.$min",
                "total_eur.$max"
              ]
            },
            "endpoint": "aggregate",
            "displayMode": "playground",
            "outputFormat": "table",
            "runPolicy": "manual"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "query",
          "title": "One product's state in one month",
          "size": "full",
          "config": {
            "query": {
              "from": "product_states",
              "where": {
                "product_sku": "SKU-PT-0563",
                "month": "2026-04"
              },
              "limit": 1
            },
            "endpoint": "query",
            "displayMode": "playground",
            "outputFormat": "table",
            "runPolicy": "manual"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "2 · Picked for you (Shop)",
      "widgets": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "title": "How it works",
          "size": "full",
          "config": {
            "content": "`_recommend` over `impressions` with the goal `purchased: true` ranks every product by the probability that *this* shopper buys it when it is shown.\n\n- `context.customer.pets` is a path through the link `impressions.context → contexts.customer → customers.pets`: a shopper with small animals gets small-animal products, with no per-pet rule in the app.\n- `context.month` is the month; `just_bought: false` ranks as if nothing had been bought yet.\n- `$p` is the probability; `$why` is its factorisation — the base rate times one lift per piece of context. Sort it by size to read it."
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "query",
          "title": "Picked for a small-animal household",
          "size": "full",
          "config": {
            "query": {
              "from": "impressions",
              "where": {
                "context.customer.pets": {
                  "$and": [
                    {
                      "$match": "small_animal"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                "context.month": "2026-04",
                "just_bought": false
              },
              "recommend": "product_sku",
              "goal": {
                "purchased": true
              },
              "select": [
                "sku",
                "name",
                "category",
                "pet_type",
                "price_eur",
                "$p",
                "$why"
              ],
              "limit": 10
            },
            "endpoint": "recommend",
            "displayMode": "playground",
            "outputFormat": "table",
            "runPolicy": "manual"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "query",
          "title": "The same, with a cage in the cart",
          "size": "full",
          "config": {
            "query": {
              "from": "impressions",
              "where": {
                "context.customer.pets": {
                  "$and": [
                    {
                      "$match": "small_animal"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                "context.month": "2026-04",
                "just_bought": false,
                "context.basket_categories": {
                  "$and": [
                    {
                      "$match": "small_animal_cage"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              },
              "recommend": "product_sku",
              "goal": {
                "purchased": true
              },
              "select": [
                "sku",
                "name",
                "category",
                "pet_type",
                "price_eur",
                "$p",
                "$why"
              ],
              "limit": 10
            },
            "endpoint": "recommend",
            "displayMode": "playground",
            "outputFormat": "table",
            "runPolicy": "manual"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "query",
          "title": "Without the pets: what is the pull of the context?",
          "size": "full",
          "config": {
            "query": {
              "from": "impressions",
              "where": {
                "context.month": "2026-04",
                "just_bought": false
              },
              "recommend": "product_sku",
              "goal": {
                "purchased": true
              },
              "select": [
                "sku",
                "name",
                "category",
                "pet_type",
                "price_eur",
                "$p",
                "$why"
              ],
              "limit": 10
            },
            "endpoint": "recommend",
            "displayMode": "playground",
            "outputFormat": "table",
            "runPolicy": "manual"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "3 · Smart search",
      "widgets": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "title": "How it works",
          "size": "full",
          "config": {
            "content": "A plain text search for `food` returns hundreds of matches in no useful order. Adding the shopper's pets and the same `_recommend` goal re-ranks the matches for *this* household: `product_sku.name` follows the link to the product and `$match` finds the word."
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "query",
          "title": "Re-rank 'food' for a dog household",
          "size": "full",
          "config": {
            "query": {
              "from": "impressions",
              "where": {
                "product_sku.name": {
                  "$match": "food"
                },
                "context.customer.pets": {
                  "$and": [
                    {
                      "$match": "dog"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                "context.month": "2026-04",
                "just_bought": false
              },
              "recommend": "product_sku",
              "goal": {
                "purchased": true
              },
              "select": [
                "sku",
                "name",
                "category",
                "pet_type",
                "price_eur",
                "$p",
                "$why"
              ],
              "limit": 10
            },
            "endpoint": "recommend",
            "displayMode": "playground",
            "outputFormat": "table",
            "runPolicy": "manual"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "4 · Bought together (cross-sell)",
      "widgets": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "title": "How it works",
          "size": "full",
          "config": {
            "content": "`orders.line_categories` lists each order's lines as `<pet>_<category>` tokens. `_relate` returns the **lift** of token co-occurrence within an order: `lift > 1` means bought together more often than chance."
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "query",
          "title": "What gets bought with dog dry-food?",
          "size": "full",
          "config": {
            "query": {
              "from": "orders",
              "where": {
                "line_categories": {
                  "$match": "dog_dryfood"
                }
              },
              "relate": "line_categories",
              "limit": 12
            },
            "endpoint": "relate",
            "displayMode": "playground",
            "outputFormat": "table",
            "runPolicy": "manual"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "5 · Churn prediction",
      "widgets": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "title": "How it works",
          "size": "full",
          "config": {
            "content": "`customer_months` holds a monthly snapshot per customer, labelled `churned_in_3_months` (true iff no order in the following three months). `_predict` returns P(true) and P(false) for a customer described by `where`; no model is trained. The evaluation widget scores the same query on held-out rows."
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "query",
          "title": "Will this customer churn?",
          "size": "full",
          "config": {
            "query": {
              "from": "customer_months",
              "where": {
                "region": "helsinki",
                "latest_sentiment": "negative",
                "latest_rating": 2,
                "had_negative_review": true
              },
              "predict": "churned_in_3_months",
              "limit": 2
            },
            "endpoint": "predict",
            "displayMode": "playground",
            "outputFormat": "table",
            "runPolicy": "manual"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "evaluate",
          "title": "How accurate is the churn prediction?",
          "size": "full",
          "config": {
            "queryType": "predict",
            "query": {
              "from": "customer_months",
              "predict": "churned_in_3_months",
              "where": {
                "region": {
                  "$get": "region"
                },
                "tenure_months_at_month": {
                  "$get": "tenure_months_at_month"
                },
                "visits": {
                  "$get": "visits"
                },
                "purchases": {
                  "$get": "purchases"
                },
                "spent_eur": {
                  "$get": "spent_eur"
                },
                "latest_sentiment": {
                  "$get": "latest_sentiment"
                },
                "had_negative_review": {
                  "$get": "had_negative_review"
                }
              }
            },
            "testSelection": {
              "type": "random",
              "percentage": 20
            }
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "6 · Product filling",
      "widgets": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "title": "How it works",
          "size": "full",
          "config": {
            "content": "A new product arrives with only a name and brand. Aito fills the rest of the record by predicting each field from the products it already knows. Change `predict` to `pet_type`, `dietary` or `tags`."
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "query",
          "title": "Predict a product's category from its name",
          "size": "full",
          "config": {
            "query": {
              "from": "products",
              "where": {
                "name": {
                  "$match": "Royal Canin Chicken Dog Food"
                },
                "brand": "Royal Canin"
              },
              "predict": "category",
              "limit": 3
            },
            "endpoint": "predict",
            "displayMode": "playground",
            "outputFormat": "table",
            "runPolicy": "manual"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "7 · Price and offers",
      "widgets": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "title": "How it works",
          "size": "full",
          "config": {
            "content": "A product's price, offer and rating in one month is a row of `product_states`. `_aggregate` gives the fair band for a SKU server-side; `_predict` over `impressions` follows the link `product_state` to ask what an offer does to the chance of a purchase."
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "query",
          "title": "Price band for one SKU",
          "size": "full",
          "config": {
            "query": {
              "from": "product_states",
              "where": {
                "product_sku": "SKU-PT-0001"
              },
              "aggregate": [
                "price_eur.$mean",
                "price_eur.$min",
                "price_eur.$max"
              ]
            },
            "endpoint": "aggregate",
            "displayMode": "playground",
            "outputFormat": "table",
            "runPolicy": "manual"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "query",
          "title": "P(purchase) when a product is shown with a 20 %+ offer",
          "size": "full",
          "config": {
            "query": {
              "from": "impressions",
              "where": {
                "product_state.discount_band": "20+"
              },
              "predict": "purchased",
              "limit": 2
            },
            "endpoint": "predict",
            "displayMode": "playground",
            "outputFormat": "table",
            "runPolicy": "manual"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "query",
          "title": "P(purchase) with no offer",
          "size": "full",
          "config": {
            "query": {
              "from": "impressions",
              "where": {
                "product_state.discount_band": "none"
              },
              "predict": "purchased",
              "limit": 2
            },
            "endpoint": "predict",
            "displayMode": "playground",
            "outputFormat": "table",
            "runPolicy": "manual"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "8 · Win-back — recommend by conversion probability",
      "widgets": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "title": "How it works",
          "size": "full",
          "config": {
            "content": "Unlike `impressions`, `winback_campaigns` records a real **outcome**: each row is a campaign send with `responded: true|false`. `_recommend` optimises that directly: which product, sent to a lapsed customer with this staple category, is most likely to be responded to."
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "query",
          "title": "Best win-back products for a lapsed dog dry-food customer",
          "size": "full",
          "config": {
            "query": {
              "from": "winback_campaigns",
              "where": {
                "customer_staple_category": "dog/dry-food",
                "recency_bucket": "90-180d",
                "product_pet_type": "dog"
              },
              "recommend": "product_sku",
              "goal": {
                "responded": true
              },
              "select": [
                "sku",
                "name",
                "category",
                "$p"
              ],
              "limit": 8
            },
            "endpoint": "recommend",
            "displayMode": "playground",
            "outputFormat": "table",
            "runPolicy": "manual"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "query",
          "title": "Calibrated response probability for one product context",
          "size": "full",
          "config": {
            "query": {
              "from": "winback_campaigns",
              "where": {
                "customer_staple_category": "dog/dry-food",
                "recency_bucket": "90-180d",
                "product_category": "dry-food",
                "product_pet_type": "dog"
              },
              "predict": "responded",
              "limit": 2
            },
            "endpoint": "predict",
            "displayMode": "playground",
            "outputFormat": "table",
            "runPolicy": "manual"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "9 · Review triage",
      "widgets": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "title": "How it works",
          "size": "full",
          "config": {
            "content": "`reviews.text` is free text. `_predict` on `category` reads it with `$match`, so a new review is routed (praise, quality, shipping, fit, question) without a rule list."
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "query",
          "title": "Which category is this review?",
          "size": "full",
          "config": {
            "query": {
              "from": "reviews",
              "where": {
                "text": {
                  "$match": "arrived late and the box was damaged"
                }
              },
              "predict": "category",
              "limit": 3
            },
            "endpoint": "predict",
            "displayMode": "playground",
            "outputFormat": "table",
            "runPolicy": "manual"
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
